<title>SWEDEN: TABLE - Scania H1 profit falls 36 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Scania H1 profit falls 36 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish truckmaker Scania reports earnings for six months ending June 30, 1997:</p>
<p>(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		1,348   vs   2,102</p>
<p> Sales				    18,941   vs  17,376</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	  5.00   vs    7.55</p>
<p> Cost of goods sold		   14,490   vs  12,601</p>
<p> R&amp;D costs				   598   vs     567</p>
<p> Sales costs			     2,253   vs   1,808</p>
<p> Administration costs		    344   vs     294</p>
<p> Interests in associates		 134   vs     157</p>
<p> Depreciation				824   vs     656</p>
<p> Operating profit			1,423   vs   2,293</p>
<p> Net financial items	   CHARGE   75   vs     191  CHARGE</p>
<p> Minorities				    0   vs	 4</p>
<p> Tax					   347   vs     594</p>
<p> Net profit				1,001   vs   1,512</p>
<p>NOTE -- Scania was expected to post a lower profit after financial items for the first half of 1997 of 1.43 billion crowns and sales were expected to increase to 18.10 billion crowns, a Reuters poll showed.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
